      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I misgender all the time, but I don't really care since for me gender not relevant for most convo I have.\nThey announced on the Dev stream last week what foreversandaday ask. A sub text below your name. Not a fan of more text in my view, but as the icon/name. You can toggle it on the fly.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "646cd70b8d9d8b090f2b1047",
      "author": {
        "_id": "63882dc1f272550ad4b6b553",
        "alias": "Nautical blue Horse",
        "aliasID": "65c26de3ed6eefce4c583e46",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/695b6d04a8df3baaf7dc5fffa66b6b56.png",
        "created": "2022-12-01T04:29:53.950Z",
        "name": "ʙɪɢ․",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2023-05-23T15:08:59.182Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "60651c265e4ffa477e53efd2",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would be a great addition! Many people put their pronouns in their bio only for them to not always get read, and not everyone is willing to sacrifice space in their status to display their pronouns.\n\nIn a deeply social environment with such a large queer population as VRChat, especially where many of those people come to feel welcome and have their identity treated with compassion, I feel like it only makes sense to have a dedicated pronoun badge under your nameplate like ForeverAndaDay mentioned to make sure people are instantly referred to in the way they feel comfortable at a glance.\n\nThis makes even more sense when you consider that VRChat's avatar culture incentivizes exploration of gender identity and it's not always clear how someone wants to be referred as. Having a pronoun badge would help mitigate this confusion significantly and I strongly believe it would make a lot of trans VRChat users, queer people in general, and even everyone else, just a touch more comfortable meeting new people :]\n\nMaking social interactions stronger through things only possible in VR is exactly what VRChat is about, and this is a perfect example of that. People shouldn't have to experience the discomfort of being misgendered if they don't need to be, considering we're in a virtual environment. I really hope this is considered for a future release :]",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
